            <ArticleTitle>Dextrocardia with asymptomatic right atrial appendage aneurysm: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1772-1774</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1150</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Right atrial appendage aneurysm (RAAA) is rarely encountered with variable intracardiac anatomy. We report a case of asymptomatic RAAA in a patient with dextrocardia and anomalous origin of RCA from left coronary sinus which was treated successfully by CABG and the aneurysm was completely excised.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
